     1. # Documentation Sync Validator Agent
     2. 
     3. > **Agent Type**: Documentation Quality & Synchronization
     4. > **Version**: 1.0.0
     5. > **Status**: 🟢 ACTIVE
     6. > **Priority**: HIGH
     7. > **Base Component**: doc-freshness-checker (75% reuse)
     8. > **Extensions**: semantic-search, config-validator
     9. 
     10. ---
     11. 
     12. ## 🎯 Purpose
     13. 
     14. Automatically validate documentation synchronization with codebase, detect semantic drift between code and docs, and ensure schema compliance across all documentation files.
     15. 
     16. ## 📋 Capabilities
     17. 
     18. - **Semantic Code-Doc Matching**: Uses vector embeddings to detect semantic drift
     19. - **Schema Validation**: Validates documentation structure and metadata
     20. - **Link Validation**: Checks all internal and external links
     21. - **Freshness Detection**: Identifies stale documentation (>90 days)
     22. - **API Doc Sync**: Ensures API docs match current implementation
     23. - **Content Drift Detection**: Detects when code changes outpace doc updates
     24. 
     25. ## 🚀 Quick Start
     26. 
     27. ### GitHub Actions Trigger
     28. 
     29. ```yaml
     30. name: Documentation Sync Validator
     31. on:
     32.   pull_request:
     33.     paths:
     34.       - 'docs/**'
     35.       - 'src/**'
     36.       - '*.md'
     37.   schedule:
     38.     - cron: '0 0 * * 0'  # Weekly on Sunday
     39.     
     40. jobs:
     41.   validate-docs:
     42.     runs-on: ubuntu-latest
     43.     steps:
     44.       - uses: actions/checkout@v4
     45.       - name: Run Documentation Sync Validator
     46.         uses: ./.github/agents/documentation-sync-validator
     47.         with:
     48.           check-freshness: true
     49.           validate-links: true
     50.           semantic-drift-threshold: 0.7
     51. ```
     52. 
     53. ### CLI Usage
     54. 
     55. ```bash
     56. # Full validation
     57. python -m documentation_sync_validator.src.agent validate --all
     58. 
     59. # Check freshness only
     60. python -m documentation_sync_validator.src.agent check-freshness docs/
     61. 
     62. # Validate specific file
     63. python -m documentation_sync_validator.src.agent validate docs/api.md
     64. 
     65. # Semantic drift analysis
     66. python -m documentation_sync_validator.src.agent semantic-check src/ docs/
     67. ```
     68. 
     69. ## 📊 Configuration
     70. 
     71. See `config/agent_config.yaml` for full configuration options:
     72. 
     73. - `freshness_threshold_days`: 90 (default)
     74. - `semantic_drift_threshold`: 0.7 (default)
     75. - `link_check_timeout`: 10 (seconds)
     76. - `enable_caching`: true
     77. 
     78. ## 📁 File Structure
     79. 
     80. ```
     81. .github/agents/documentation-sync-validator/
     82. ├── README.md                    # This file
     83. ├── CHANGELOG.md                 # Version history
     84. ├── agent.yaml                   # GitHub Actions integration
     85. ├── config/
     86. │   └── agent_config.yaml       # Configuration with cognitive brain
     87. ├── prompts/
